WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.871
Fleet management begins with an authoritative inventory of aircraft, controllers, batteries, payloads, chargers, accessories, firmware, ownership, location, and status.

00:00:09.871 --> 00:00:14.927
Each asset needs a unique identifier and responsible custodian.

00:00:14.927 --> 00:00:24.317
Maintenance logs capture inspections, flight hours or cycles where relevant, defects, repairs, parts, updates, incidents, and return-to-service approval.

00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:31.299
Records should show the configuration that actually flew, not only the model purchased.

00:00:31.299 --> 00:00:39.726
Batteries need individual tracking because age, cycles, storage, temperature, damage, swelling, and voltage behavior affect safety.

00:00:39.726 --> 00:00:47.671
A battery should not inherit an aircraft's general ready status without its own condition review.

00:00:47.671 --> 00:00:52.245
Preflight inspections confirm readiness for the specific mission.

00:00:52.245 --> 00:00:59.227
Post-flight inspections look for damage, contamination, heat, unusual sound, impact, or performance changes.

00:00:59.227 --> 00:01:04.283
Findings should enter a repair or grounding workflow immediately.

00:01:04.283 --> 00:01:07.895
Firmware and application updates require governance.

00:01:07.895 --> 00:01:15.840
Record versions, review significant changes, test as appropriate, and avoid unplanned configuration drift across crews.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:22.340
Updating everything immediately before a critical mission can create its own risk.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.470
Ground unsafe or uncertain equipment.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:31.489
Mission urgency, sunk cost, and spare shortages do not change airworthiness.

00:01:31.489 --> 00:01:38.953
Lifecycle management should anticipate obsolescence, unsupported software, repair lead time, replacement, and secure retirement.

00:01:38.953 --> 00:01:45.935
Maintain an approved configuration baseline for aircraft, controller, application, payload, and critical settings.

00:01:45.935 --> 00:01:55.324
A replacement component or reset may look ready while silently changing return behavior, units, storage, or warning thresholds.
